19. WNC Improved Word + Character TF-IDF Linear SVM

A second WNC approach was evaluated using a Linear Support Vector Machine with combined word-level and character-level TF-IDF features.

The word-level representation used unigram and bigram features with a maximum of 50,000 features.

The character-level representation used character n-grams from 3 to 5 characters with a maximum of 30,000 features.

Word TF-IDF configuration:

ngram_range = (1,2)
min_df = 2
max_df = 0.95
sublinear_tf = True
max_features = 50,000

Character TF-IDF configuration:

ngram_range = (3,5)
min_df = 2
max_df = 0.95
sublinear_tf = True
max_features = 30,000

Linear SVM configuration:

C = 1.0
class_weight = balanced

The development-set results were:

Metric                 Result
Accuracy               69.47%
Macro Precision        69.48%
Macro Recall           69.48%
Macro F1               69.47%

The development Macro F1 comparison was:

Model                                      Dev Macro F1
TF-IDF + Logistic Regression               67.88%
Word + Character TF-IDF + Linear SVM       69.47%

Because the Word + Character TF-IDF + Linear SVM produced the higher development Macro F1, it was selected for final held-out test evaluation.


