Sentiment output
Evidence output
Argument-quality output

This creates a consistent representation that can later be transmitted through the FastAPI backend and WebSocket connection.


30.3 SVM Decision Strength

The trained Linear SVM classifiers do not naturally produce probability values.

Therefore, their raw decision-function margins are not presented as probabilities.

For internal review-oriented scoring, BiasLess converts the absolute SVM margin into a bounded decision-strength indicator:

decision_strength = |margin| / (1 + |margin|)

The resulting value lies between 0 and 1.

This value is called Decision Strength rather than Confidence or Probability because it is derived from the SVM decision margin and is not a calibrated probability.


