33. Near-Real-Time Speech Processing Architecture

With the text-based NLP engine successfully integrated, the project progressed to the complete audio-to-speech processing pipeline.

The speech processing architecture consists of:

Microphone / Browser Audio Input (MediaRecorder WebM/Opus)
        ↓
PyAV Audio Decoding & 16 kHz Mono Normalization
        ↓
Voice Activity Detection (Silero VAD)
        ↓
Speech Region Extraction & Audio Anti-Clipping
        ↓
faster-whisper Local Speech-to-Text (CPU, INT8)
        ↓
ASR Corruption & Speech Quality Gating (content_gate.py)
        ↓
Completed Text Utterance & Context Pairing
        ↓
ReasonIQ NLP Engine (Fallacy, Argument, Bias, Sentiment, Evidence)
        ↓
Authoritative Scoring & Deduction Breakdown
        ↓
FastAPI Backend & Real-Time WebSocket Streaming
        ↓
React Dashboard & Real-Time Audio Waveform Cards
        ↓
Post-Debate Comprehensive Report Service (JSON / PDF)

The system operates in near-real-time locally on CPU without requiring cloud speech APIs or paid external services.


33.1 Configurable Speech-to-Text Implementation

